              actually WRITE sees ONE (systemd, on kubelet's instruction), collapsing the race to a
              precedence-among-sources question --- so the care-count framing and the write-count
              framing DIVERGE, and a genuine two-independent-writer control DOES have a real race,
              proving the collapse is caused by the single writer, not by the reasoning being lax},
  verdict  = {AGREES},
  check    = {witness:who-wins-last-write-two-writers}
}

